    Odoo 19 note: mail.BaseRecipientsList was removed from mail core, together with
    the whole read-only "recipient summary span + caret button opening a popover"
    layout it belonged to (see mail/.../core/web/base_recipients_list.xml on the 18.0
    branch). It was replaced by mail.RecipientsInput (mail/.../core/web/
    recipients_input.{js,xml}), a self-contained live tags-input row now used
    directly by mail.Chatter (mail/.../chatter/web/chatter.xml):

        <div class="d-flex py-1 ps-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 text-end fw-bold px-2" style="width:46px">To: </span>
            <RecipientsInput thread="state.thread"/>
        </div>

    This extension used to xpath //button/.. (the <span> wrapping BaseRecipientsList's
    summary text + caret button) to strip a stray "style" attribute and add
    "o-mail-Chatter-recipientList", a class chatter.scss used purely to mirror the
    responsive margin-left of the sibling ".o-mail-SuggestedRecipient" element
    (0 on xs, 42px from sm) so the two rows stayed visually aligned.

    Neither counterpart exists in the new layout: mail.RecipientsInput has no <button>
    to xpath onto, and ".o-mail-SuggestedRecipient" (SuggestedRecipientsList) was
    removed from mail core entirely - grep across
    addons/mail/static/src/ on the 19.0 branch returns no match for either symbol.
    The new row already aligns itself via its own fixed-width "To:" label column and
    flex layout, so there is no clean landing spot left to preserve the old
    responsive-indent intent onto - reapplying the same margin-left toggle onto
    mail.RecipientsInput's root would only misalign it against the label. This
    extension's effect - and the now-dead ".o-mail-Chatter-recipientList" SCSS rules -
    are therefore intentionally dropped (see chatter.scss).
-->
